messages:  ["Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 849845 and 612536? Please reason step by step.\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the sum of 849845 and 612536, we need to follow these steps:\n1. Align the numbers by their place values, making sure the digits in the same place value are in the same column.\n2. Add the digits starting from the rightmost column (units place) and move to the left.\n3. If the sum in any column is 10 or more, carry over the tens digit to the next column to the left.\n4. Continue this process until all columns have been added.\n</think>\n<answer>\nLet's perform the addition step by step:\n```\n  849845\n+ 612536\n---------\n```\nStarting from the rightmost column (units place):\n5 + 6 = 11. Write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n```\n  849845\n+ 612536\n---------\n      1\n```\nNext column (tens place):\n4 + 3 + 1 (carried over) = 8. Write down 8.\n```\n  849845\n+ 612536\n---------\n     81\n```\nNext column (hundreds place):\n8 + 5 = 13. Write down 3 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n```\n  849845\n+ 612536\n---------\n    381\n```\nNext column (thousands place):\n9 + 2 + 1 (carried over) = 12. Write down 2 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n```\n  849845\n+ 612536\n---------\n   2381\n```\nNext column (ten thousands place):\n4 + 1 = 5. Write down 5.\n```\n  849845\n+ 612536\n---------\n  52381\n```\nNext column (hundred thousands place):\n8 + 6 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n```\n  849845\n+ 612536\n---------\n 452381\n```\nFinally, the leftmost column (millions place):\n1 + 0 = 1. Write down 1.\n```\n  849845\n+ 612536\n---------\n1462381\n```\nTherefore, the sum of 849845 and 612536 is 1462381.\n</answer>\n"]
