  "model": "Qwen2.5-3B-SFT-GRPO-400",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "Continuing with the next place values:\n   - 2 + 6 = 8\n   - So, we write down 8 in the thousands place of the sum.\n   - 4 + 1 = 5\n   - So, we write down 5 in the ten-thousands place of the sum.\n   - 5 + 8 = 13\n   - Since 13 is a two-digit number, we write down 3 in the hundred-thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n8. Finally, we have the millions place:\n   - 0 (from 542621) + 8 (from 861111) + 1 (carried over) = 9\n   - So, we write down 9 in the millions place of the sum.\n9. Putting it all together, the sum is:\n   ```\n   542621\n   +861111\n   ------\n   1403732\n   ```\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe sum of 542621 and 861111 is 1403732.\n</answer>",
