n is correct. Let's do it step by step:\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (units place):\n2 + 8 = 10. Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n```\n  943652\n+ 340758\n---------\n      0\n```\nNext column (tens place):\n5 + 5 + 1 (carried over) = 11. Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n```\n  943652\n+ 340758\n---------\n      1\n```\nNext column (hundreds place):\n6 + 7 + 1 (carried over) = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1.\n```\n  943652\n+ 340758\n---------\n     41\n```\nNext column (thousands place):\n3 + 0 + 1 (carried over) = 4.\n```\n  943652\n+ 340758\n---------\n    414\n```\nNext column (ten thousands place):\n4 + 4 = 8.\n```\n  943652\n+ 340758\n---------\n   8414\n```\nNext column (hundred thousands place):\n9 + 3 = 12. Write down 2 and carry over 1.\n```\n  943652\n+ 340758\n---------\n 128414\n```\nFinally, the leftmost column (millions place):\n1 + 0 = 1.\n```\n  943652\n+ 340758\n---------\n1284140\n```\nThe result of the addition is 1284140, which is not the number we started with (1284400). This confirms that there was an error in the original addition. The correct sum should be 1284140, not 1284400. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>I see the mistake now. Thank you for walking me through the subtraction and rechecking the addition. This really helps in understanding the process.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! Understanding the process of addition and subtraction, and how to verify the results, is crucial for developing strong mathematical skills. If you have any more questions or need further clarification, feel free to ask. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for your help. I feel much more confident in my ability to solve and verify addition problems now.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're very welcome! I'm glad to hear that you feel more confident. Remember, practice is key to mastering these skills. If you have any more questions or need further assistance, don't hesitate to ask. Good luck with your studies! <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you. I'll keep practicing and seeking